{
  "id": "I-0343",
  "kind": "issue",
  "audience": "human",
  "scope": {},
  "title": "TWO TEAMS PROVED THE SAME KEYSTONE LEMMA CONCURRENTLY — A COORDINATION GAP WORTH A DECISION (2026-07-25).",
  "body": "TWO TEAMS PROVED THE SAME KEYSTONE LEMMA CONCURRENTLY — A COORDINATION GAP WORTH A DECISION (2026-07-25).\n\nWHAT HAPPENED. Run 0047 session 0014 (me) and a later run's session on the SAME task\n(ajcr-w4-rep-free) were live on the workspace simultaneously. Both read Ground's I-0334, both\nidentified the same missing keystone ((c1) forces leak-freeness), and both proved it by the same\nroute (finiteness => Spec finite over the base => universally closed => cancel against the SEPARATED\nambient => closed map => the trace is closed). Two files, one fact:\n  - theirs: DivSchemeCertZarC1.lean (isClosed_zeroLocus_inter_of_finite_quotient,\n    supportLeak_eq_empty_iff_finite_colength, supportLocus_subset_chart_of_isCertified)\n  - mine:  DivSchemeCertZarConverse.lean (isClosed_zeroLocus_of_finite_quotient,\n    supportLeak_eq_empty_of_finite_colength, IsCertified.forall_supportLeak_eq_empty)\nI deleted mine (commit 7f29687ca) since theirs is strictly richer (an iff, plus the composed\nverdict) and kept only the piece neither had: the obstruction in witness form\n(not_isCertified_of_isPreconnected_of_witnesses). No work was lost and the build is green (9078\njobs), but roughly a session's worth of compute was spent twice.\n\nWHY IT HAPPENED, and it is not the agents' fault. The horizon skill says teams coordinate through\nshared state, and we did read it -- but the shared state had no marker for 'a keystone lemma is\nbeing proved right now'. The roadmap records ITEMS, not in-flight lemmas; the inbox item that\ntriggered us both (I-0334) is an issue describing work to do, with no claim mechanism. Two teams on\nthe SAME task id is the aggravating factor: nothing in the CLI warns 'another run holds your task',\nonly 'another run is live on this workspace'.\n\nSUGGESTIONS, for you to decide:\n (a) do not schedule two runs on the same task id concurrently, or\n (b) give inbox items an explicit claim/owner (like roadmap --owner) so 'I am proving I-0334 now' is\n     recordable, and have the synchronizer digest warn when another live run shares your task id.\n\nAlso worth noting: rounds 1-5 of run 0047 produced empty reports and zero Lean commits (~206 USD).\nRounds 0 and 6 did all the work. That looks like a harness fault rather than agent behaviour, and it\nis the larger waste of the two. A separate report (I-0333) raised the same point.",
